        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The conventional method of spinning core yarns using a ring spinning frame is reported to produce uneven looping of the core yarn which influences detrimentally the yarn quality. This method is also claimed to be inefficient since in wrapping the core filament with the loosened fibrous material an additional twist is imparted to the core yarn. These problems are not apparent when the open-end rotor spinning procedure is applied to core yarn spinning. 

The advantages of a rotor spinning machine are higher production, low hairiness, more even yarn with good bulkiness. The strength of the rotor yarn is less when compared with ring spun yarn but the coefficient of variation in strength is very less2. Three methods are followed in this regard to produce the core yarn in rotor spinning machine.

Twist efficiency and pre-tension of filament are the influencing factors in core spinning. In order to increase the contact area between yarn arm and doffing tube (for increasing the twist efficiency), a copper flange was soldered to the inner end of the doffing tube. The doffing tube was mounted on a ball bearing, rotated by a separate drive opposite to the rotation of the rotor with a speed ratio of 1:9. The rotating doffing tube inserts a false twist and pushes twist back to the peel-off point. The rotation of rotor wraps the yarn arm around the continuous filament core. A minimum pre-tension is necessary to avoid filament flung out in to the rotor-collecting surface. The core is not twisted during this process. It is economical to produce coarse core-spun yarns through rotor machine than the ring core-spun yarns.

The model represents the process itself, hence the input raw materials are not included in the model. The user will use this dataset along with the input raw materials. Energy uses and infrastructure are included in the model. There is no direct emission to soil and air since the emission comes from electricity usage, while the hazardous waste comes from waste lube oil. In the model, enegy sources of machine is used solely from electricity. The machine used in this model is the rotor spinning machine. The consumption of lubricating oil using a thermobonding oven as a proxy. 

Fibre2Fashion (2021) Methods of Producing Core Spun Yarn in Rotor Spinning https://www.fibre2fashion.com/industry-article/4846/methods-of-producing-core-spun-yarn-in-rotor-spinning  

Fibre2Fashion (2021) Production and Properties of Core Spun Yarns https://www.fibre2fashion.com/industry-article/1764/production-and-properties-of-core-spun-yarns</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
